`]}),e.jsxs(a,{title:"The semester in six phases",children:[e.jsx(t.p,{children:"The 14 weeks fall into six phases."}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Orientation is Week 1: the language-model objective, tokens and the environment. The Foundation phase, Weeks 2 to 4, builds the decoder block, then multi-head attention with rotary position embedding (RoPE), then modern attention. Training at Scale, Weeks 5 to 8, covers optimization, parallelization, scaling and data. Advanced Systems, Weeks 9 to 11, covers mixture of experts (MoE), architecture experiments and inference. Post-Training, Weeks 12 and 13, covers supervised fine-tuning (SFT), direct preference optimization (DPO) and on-policy reinforcement learning (RL). The Capstone, Week 14, synthesizes the course and holds the last project pitches. You pitch your final-project idea in a tutorial whenever you are ready, and Week 14 is the latest."}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Coding exercises run from Week 2 through Week 13, one per week, twelve in all, and each extends the same codebase. Exercises are pass/fail. Passing any six of the twelve qualifies you for the final project."})]})]}),e.jsxs(s,{title:"The reading is mandatory",accent:2,number:"16",items:"5",children:[e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
