`]}),e.jsxs(a,{title:"What it takes to be productive from day 1",children:[e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Being productive from day 1 takes four things."}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"You practice in the loop that this course runs every week. You start from a specification, build an implementation, test and measure it, and use the feedback from the tutorial to decide what to change next. The loop closes the gap between knowing about a system and being able to diagnose one. All of the work extends one config-driven codebase over 14 weeks. Week 1 sets up the concepts and the environment, and nothing is due this week."}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"You know where the field stands. Its core architecture, the Transformer, dates from 2017. Since then the field has moved fast, through seven eras from the Transformer to today's agents, and this course builds a piece of most of them."}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"You derisk every decision before you scale it. Reasoning alone cannot tell you whether a change helps, so you declare the experiment before the run. You state a hypothesis and test one intended change against a trusted baseline, with a matched budget of tokens and compute. You fix the evaluation set and a validated metric, plan a noise check, and declare in advance the threshold for scaling up, revising or stopping. When every run is expensive, this is how a few runs still give you a reliable answer."}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"And you understand the one objective that everything else builds on. A tokenizer cuts text into pieces and maps each piece to an integer ID, and each ID selects one row of the embedding table. How the tokenizer segments text changes the sequence length, and its vocabulary size changes the size of the embedding table and the output layer. Bonus 1, which is required reading, covers tokenization in depth. At every position the model produces logits, and softmax turns them into a distribution over the vocabulary. The chain rule factors the probability of a sequence into next-token probabilities, an exact identity, and training minimizes the cross-entropy loss, the mean negative log-probability of the realized next tokens."}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"That is the goal of this course: to be productive from day 1. The next 14 weeks build the skills it takes. Week 2 turns the next-token objective into one trainable Transformer block."})]})]}),e.jsx(s,{title:"To-dos until next week",accent:1,number:"35",children:e.jsxs("div",{className:"flex flex-col gap-10",children:[e.jsxs("div",{className:"flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-x-24 gap-y-6",children:[e.jsxs("figure",{className:"text-center",children:[e.jsx("a",{href:"https://tally.so/r/Zj44x0",children:e.jsx("img",{src:"images/qr-week-01-muddiest-point.svg",alt:"QR code for the muddiest-point survey, tally.so/r/Zj44x0",className:"w-56 h-56"})}),e.jsxs("figcaption",{children:[e.jsx("strong",{children:"Muddiest point"}),e.jsx("br",{}),"Do it right now! (2 min)"]})]}),e.jsxs("figure",{className:"text-center",children:[e.jsx("a",{href:"https://tally.so/r/e5ZZBk",children:e.jsx("img",{src:"images/qr-intro-survey.svg",alt:"QR code for the intro survey, tally.so/r/e5ZZBk",className:"w-56 h-56"})}),e.jsxs("figcaption",{children:[e.jsx("strong",{children:"Intro survey"}),e.jsx("br",{}),"Do it at home."]})]})]}),e.jsxs("div",{className:"grid gap-x-12 gap-y-6 md:grid-cols-2",children:[e.jsxs("div",{children:[e.jsx("div",{className:"font-semibold",children:"Once you have a spot in the class"}),e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
